description:
Masters or PhD degree in Mathematics, Physics, Hydrogeological Sciences or Geological / Civil / Environmental / Mining Engineering or related field;
With Minimum 4 to 9 years if experience.
Experience in numerical analyses for engineering applications;
An understanding of numerical methods including finite difference, finite element and control volume finite element approaches;
Proficiency in the use of commercial numerical groundwater modelling codes is an asset (FEFLOW, MODFLOW, HydroGeoSphere, etc.);
Experience with visualization software (GIS, Surfer, Leapfrog, CAD, etc.);
Experience with general-purpose scripting/programming is an asset (Python, VBA, etc.);
Experience in global optimization and developing complex 3D geometries for numerical modelling purposes;
Experience with parameter estimation and global optimization software;
Understanding of data science and analytics, and practical applications in the field of hydrogeology;
Direct exposure to machine learning would be an asset;
Some understanding and experience with physical hydrogeology would be an asset;
Demonstrates critical analytical and strong written and verbal communication skills.
Experience with Microsoft Office software suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.).
Self-motivated, curious and well organized;
Ability to work in a team environment.
BGV:
Employment with WSP India is subject to the successful completion of a background verification ( BGV ) check conducted by a third-party agency appointed by WSP India.
Candidates are advised to ensure that all information provided during the recruitment process including documents uploaded is accurate and complete, both to WSP India and its BGV partner .

